changes in diabetic patients</article-title><source>Clin Chim Acta</source><year>2004</year><volume>346</volume><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15256317</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-15-br-0219"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynolds</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hyperglycemia-induced ascorbic acid deficiency promotes endothelial dysfunction and the development of atherosclerosis</article-title><source>Atherosclerosis</source><year>2001</year><volume>158</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11500168</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-15-br-0219"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peerapatdit</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Likidlilid</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Patchanans</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Somkasetrin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antioxidant status and lipid peroxidation end products in patients of type 1 diabetes mellitus</article-title><source>J Med Assoc Thai</source><year>2006</year><volume>89 </volume><issue>Suppl 5</issue><fpage>S141</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17718255</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-15-br-0219"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kamal-Eldin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Appelqvist</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The chemistry and antioxidant properties of tocopherols and tocotrienols</article-title><source>Lipids</source><year>1996</year><volum